Mouse
· Pointing at a row, an entry or a key of the footer only highlights it.
  Click a row to select it, double click to open it, use the wheel to
  scroll and click a key of the footer to press it.
· Drag to select text, it is copied when you release the button.
  Shift+drag selects with the terminal instead (Option+drag in iTerm2),
  then Ctrl+Shift+C copies.
· With ui.mouse off, the terminal selects text itself and Ctrl+Shift+C
  works as usual.

Safety: [ctrl+c] goes back and never quits at once, [ctrl+d] quits, and
nothing is lost on quit because every write is immediate. What is not
saved yet, such as a form, is asked about first.
Unin
